======
 ddm
======

---
DDM
---

:Date: Dec 2025
:Version: ddm @DDM_VERSION@
:Manual section: 1
:Manual group: ddm

SYNOPSIS
========

ddm [OPTIONS...]

DESCRIPTION
===========

ddm is a display and login manager based on Qt technologies and using
Treeland as greeter.

If pam and systemd are available, the greeter will go through logind,
which will give it access to drm devices.

Distributions without pam and systemd will need to put the **ddm** user
into the **video** group, otherwise errors regarding GL and drm devices
might be experienced.

For X11 sessions, the cookie for X authorization is written into a
temporary file `/tmp/xauth_XXXXXX`, owned and only accessible by the
user.

OPTIONS
=======

--test-mode
	Start daemon in test mode.

--example-config
	Print the complete current configuration to stdout

--help, -h
	Show help message and exit.

FILES
=====

DDM stores its configuration through the DConfig framework of the Deepin
Desktop Environment, under the application id ``org.deepin.dde.ddm``. The
corresponding schemas are installed in **@DDM_DCONFIG_DIR@**:

**@DDM_DCONFIG_META_FILE@**
	Schema describing the DDM configuration options.

**@DDM_DCONFIG_STATE_FILE@**
	Schema describing the last user and session state.

The effective values are kept by the DConfig daemon and can be read or
changed with the ``dde-dconfig`` tool. See **ddm.conf**\(5\) for the
complete list of options.

SEE ALSO
